{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if the household be too little for a lamb.</b> That is, if the members of the household are too few to have a single lamb for themselves, for they cannot consume it and it would come to the state of נותר (leftover)." "<b>He and his neighbor shall take.</b> The Torah shows concern for the property of Israel in four places. The first is here, for since leftover stands to be burned, therefore the Torah was concerned for you beforehand and said, ״ואם ימעט הבית מהיות משה ולקח הוא ושכנו״ — so that you not lose your money. The second (Leviticus 7), ״וחלב נבלה וחלב טרפה יעשה לכל מלאכה ואכול לא תאכלוהו״. The third is what is written regarding נבלה (Deuteronomy 14), ״לגר אשר בשעריך תתננה ואכלה או מכור לנכרי״. The fourth is the plague-stricken house, as it says (Leviticus 14), ״וצוה הכהן ופנו את הבית״ — because if the dyed garments are washed they will be ruined and their color will fade, and likewise an earthen vessel, if it became impure, has no remedy except through breaking; therefore the Torah showed concern and said, ״ופנו את הבית״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:01.934562201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}